error[Z0219]: `z = NA` has no type
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | w.add(z = NA)
  |           ^^ NA alone
  |
  = help: a variable of only NA needs a type: build it from one of the frame's, as in `x * NA`; `to(NA, Float)` arrives with release 0.5.0

error[Z0401]: `add` defines columns from a Column, Bool, Int, Float or Str, but `z` is a List<Int>
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:11
  |
2 | w.add(z = [1, 2, 3])
  |           ^^^^^^^^^ a List<Int>
  |
  = help: usage: `data.add(name = Column | Bool | Int | Float | Str, ...)`

error[Z0217]: `z` has 1 row and the frame has 3 rows
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:11
  |
3 | w.add(z = o["x"])
  |           ^^^^^^ a column of another length
  |
  = help: build the new variable from the frame's own variables; `merge` joins frames (release 0.6.0)

